1
00:00:00,138 --> 00:00:01,468
I was on the radio once.

2
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:03,720
I called into Fever 104 FM New Delhi...

3
00:00:03,934 --> 00:00:06,894
...and was the fourth person
to say the phrase that pays:

4
00:00:07,062 --> 00:00:08,232
"Fever 104:"

5
00:00:08,397 --> 00:00:09,977
[SPEAKS IN HINDI]

6
00:00:12,693 --> 00:00:16,943
That means "Fever 104:
Home of the really good current music."

7
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:22,240
It's much catchier in Hindi.

8
00:00:23,745 --> 00:00:29,375
(Sheldon:)All right, these are the talking points
for my NPR interview tomorrow.

9
00:00:29,543 --> 00:00:31,673
(Sheldon:)I need to make
sure they're simple enough...

10
00:00:31,837 --> 00:00:35,047
(Sheldon:)...for the less educated in the audience
to understand.

11
00:00:35,674 --> 00:00:38,594
(Sheldon:)Howard, look this over
and tell me what's unclear to you.

12
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:42,890
I have a Master's in engineering from the
Massachusetts Institute of Technology.

13
00:00:43,056 --> 00:00:47,396
(Howard:)It required the completion of 144 units
of grad work and an original thesis.

14
00:00:47,853 --> 00:00:49,853
(Sheldon:)Yes.

15
00:00:50,022 --> 00:00:52,352
(Sheldon:)Look this over
and tell me what's unclear to you.

16
00:00:54,693 --> 00:00:58,113
(Leonard:)You know, when Sheldon gives you
homework, you don't have to do it.

17
00:00:58,905 --> 00:01:03,025
(Raj:)In fact, it's better if you don't.
Otherwise, the rest of us look bad.

